3971771/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3,3)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea2b88d8ce76373c23a9abc7586bc9b41532e6fd4e1ae47eb3fb175e649416f1" "basis" 662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/assets/0405790e07a49ddb62c4444ba13669ee74e6b7c37d5c2949a244246b8d54b65a.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea2b88d8ce76373c23a9abc7586bc9b41532e6fd4e1ae47eb3fb175e649416f1" "basis" 662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(5,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea2b88d8ce76373c23a9abc7586bc9b41532e6fd4e1ae47eb3fb175e649416f1" "basis" 662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "137eb9aea9d33d7ab5b15f390222fa52430076aa2c0d657a7dd6401ae8ed8f74" "basis" 662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278312" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea2b88d8ce76373c23a9abc7586bc9b41532e6fd4e1ae47eb3fb175e649416f1" "basis" 662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278312" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{(x-5)^2}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^2}{25}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea2b88d8ce76373c23a9abc7586bc9b41532e6fd4e1ae47eb3fb175e649416f1" "basis" 662 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971771/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{81}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/state.json" "file_sha256" "7fa7bb211817ee62f856a7dab7c884db5d65bb38d660a4e8119b8e896b812d87" "basis" 892 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=3$ and $k=-8,$ so the center is located at $(3,-8).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=8$ and ${b}^{2}=81.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=8,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=81,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{81}=9.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=9,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 9=18,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/state.json" "file_sha256" "7fa7bb211817ee62f856a7dab7c884db5d65bb38d660a4e8119b8e896b812d87" "basis" 892 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "62dce0bec929801edebfbbf1fe08dc7eb7131a05544044744aa1ad1420d64268" "basis" 892 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "